# Copy this file to dashboard/.env.local and fill in real values.
# .env.local is gitignored AND blocked by the pre-commit secret guard — never commit it.
#
# On Vercel these same four names go in Project Settings -> Environment Variables,
# with the project's Root Directory set to `dashboard`.

# --- Supabase Auth ---------------------------------------------------------
# Since Phase 2a the dashboard has real accounts: any Google user with a
# verified address can sign up, and Supabase Auth issues the session. There is
# no allowlist any more — ALLOWED_EMAIL, AUTH_SECRET and the GOOGLE_* pair are
# all gone, along with Auth.js itself.
#
# The Google OAuth client's authorised redirect URI is now SUPABASE's, not this
# app's:
#   https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
# The client id and secret go into the Supabase dashboard (Authentication ->
# Sign In / Providers -> Google), NOT into this file — which is why neither
# appears below.
#
# Supabase -> Authentication -> URL Configuration must list, exactly and with no
# wildcards, the places a session may be delivered:
#   http://localhost:3000/auth/callback
#   https://<your-vercel-domain>/auth/callback
#
# Both values below are NEXT_PUBLIC_ and are therefore INLINED AT BUILD TIME
# into the browser bundle. They must exist on Vercel BEFORE the deploy that
# needs them — added afterwards, the build has `undefined` baked in and fails
# as a broken client rather than as a missing variable.
#
# The anon key is meant to be public, but only because RLS stands behind it.
# That had to be MADE true here: until 2a seven of this database's ten tables
# had RLS off with anon holding full DML. db/schema.sql's RLS block closed it;
# `python scripts/check_rls.py` reads the answer back. There is deliberately NO
# service-role key anywhere in this app — every read and write of this project's
# own data goes through DASHBOARD_DB_URL below.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<the anon / publishable key from Project Settings -> API>

# --- Outbound contact address, AND who you are -----------------------------
# Two jobs, and the second one is why this is now REQUIRED rather than merely
# polite:
#
#   1. It goes into the User-Agent the "add a company" probe sends to ATS
#      boards, so a board owner who sees us in their logs can reach a human.
#      That path still falls back to unknown@example.com (src/lib/ats.ts).
#   2. It names the OPERATOR for the headless scripts. db-check, match-parity
#      and badge-check run from a terminal with no request and no session, so
#      they resolve public.users WHERE lower(email) = lower(MY_EMAIL) through
#      src/lib/currentUser.ts — the same lookup db/users.py makes on the Python
#      side, so the two runtimes agree about who you are.
#
# PHASE 2a NARROWED THIS. It is no longer how the app decides whose data to
# show: pages and routes take the user from the Supabase session and thread the
# id down (src/lib/guard.ts). A request path that still read this variable would
# serve the operator's filter and watch list to whichever stranger was signed
# in. tests/test_dashboard_auth.py asserts none of them do.
#
# 2b deletes what is left, together with db/users.py's half.
#
# Same value and same purpose as MY_EMAIL in ../.env, which the Python crawler
# reads; the dashboard needs its own copy because Vercel deploys with Root
# Directory set to `dashboard` and never sees the parent .env. SET IT ON VERCEL.
#
# Server-side only — deliberately NOT prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_, so it is never
# shipped to the browser.
MY_EMAIL=you@example.com

# --- Database --------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase TRANSACTION pooler, port 6543 (not 5432 — that is the session pooler
# the Python crawler uses). Transaction mode hands a connection back to the pool
# after every transaction, which is what a serverless dashboard wants and is
# also why prepared statements are disabled in src/lib/db.ts. Same database as
# CRAWLER_DB_URL in ../.env, different port and different pooling mode.
DASHBOARD_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# --- Optional --------------------------------------------------------------
# Where `npm run ui-check` points its unauthenticated gate assertions. Defaults
# to http://localhost:3000, which is what `npm run dev` serves.
# UI_CHECK_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
